---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Try it"
description: "Try Ferrite in your browser: the firmware's own screen code, running on a pretend radio. Nothing is sent anywhere."
---
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="page-head try-head">
    <h1>Try it</h1>
    <p class="lead">The firmware's own screen code, running in your browser on a pretend radio. Nothing is sent
      anywhere.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="sim" id="sim" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="sim-screen">
      <canvas id="screen" width="480" height="640" aria-label="The radio's screen"></canvas>
      <p class="sim-msg" id="sim-msg">Loading the radio…</p>
      <noscript><p class="sim-msg">The simulator needs JavaScript.</p></noscript>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-keys" aria-label="The radio's keys">
      <div class="keyrow side">
        <button type="button" data-key="22">PTT A</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="23">PTT B</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="20">SIDE1</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="21">SIDE2</button>
      </div>
      <div class="keyrow knob">
        <button type="button" data-knob="-1" aria-label="Knob left">◀ Knob</button>
        <button type="button" data-knob="1" aria-label="Knob right">Knob ▶</button>
      </div>
      <div class="pad nav">
        <button type="button" data-key="12" class="k-menu">MENU<small>OK</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="16" class="k-up" aria-label="Up">▲</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="15" class="k-back">BACK</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="18" class="k-left" aria-label="Left">◀</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="17" class="k-down" aria-label="Down">▼</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="19" class="k-right" aria-label="Right">▶</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="13" class="k-slot">SLOT<small>A·B·C</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="14" class="k-vm">V/M</button>
      </div>
      <div class="pad digits">
        <button type="button" data-key="1">1</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="2">2<small>ABC</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="3">3<small>DEF</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="4">4<small>GHI</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="5">5<small>JKL</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="6">6<small>MNO</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="7">7<small>PQRS</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="8">8<small>TUV</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="9">9<small>WXYZ</small></button>
        <button type="button" data-key="10">*</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="0">0</button>
        <button type="button" data-key="11">#</button>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Hold a key as you would on the radio: a long press is 0.7 seconds.</p>
      <div class="keyrow tools">
        <button type="button" id="reset" class="plain">Reset the radio</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section try-more">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Things to try</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><kbd>MENU</kbd> opens quick settings for the slot in front. Hold it for the full menu.</li>
        <li><kbd>SLOT</kbd> brings slot A, B or C to the front. Hold it to edit the slot in place.</li>
        <li>Hold <kbd>1</kbd> for the band scope.</li>
        <li><kbd>MENU</kbd> <kbd>0</kbd> <kbd>5</kbd> <kbd>3</kbd>, then the knob, turns APRS mode on.</li>
        <li>Hold <kbd>BACK</kbd> to go home from anywhere.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>On a keyboard</h2>
      <p>Click the screen first. <kbd>0</kbd>–<kbd>9</kbd> digits, <kbd>Enter</kbd> MENU/OK, <kbd>Esc</kbd> BACK,
        arrows, <kbd>,</kbd> and <kbd>.</kbd> for <kbd>*</kbd> and <kbd>#</kbd>, <kbd>S</kbd> SLOT, <kbd>V</kbd> V/M,
        <kbd>Q</kbd> and <kbd>W</kbd> SIDE1 and SIDE2, <kbd>Space</kbd> PTT A, <kbd>[</kbd> <kbd>]</kbd> or the mouse
        wheel for the knob.</p>
      <p class="note">The radio part is pretend: nothing is received or transmitted, and the stations you see are made
        up. Your settings and channels are kept in this browser only. Reset brings back the sample radio.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
<script src="/assets/try.js" defer></script>
